        "body": "## Summary\n- Normalize known numeric long flags when a negative numeric value is provided as the following space-separated token before Kong parses args.\n- Add mock-server CLI regressions for search, nearby, autocomplete, and directions using negative longitude/coordinate examples.\n- Preserve existing --flag=value behavior and normal invalid numeric errors.\n\nFixes https://github.com/openclaw/goplaces/issues/17\n\n## Validation\n- go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestNormalizeNegativeNumericFlagArgs|TestRunSearchAcceptsSpaceSeparatedNegativeLongitude|TestRunNearbyAcceptsSpaceSeparatedNegativeLongitude|TestRunAutocompleteAcceptsSpaceSeparatedNegativeLongitude|TestRunDirectionsAcceptsSpaceSeparatedNegativeCoordinates' -count=1\n- go test ./...\n\n## Credit\nReported by @technicalpickles in https://github.com/openclaw/goplaces/issues/17.\n",
